# Third-party content and attribution

This repository's own code and documents are licensed under Apache-2.0 (see `LICENSE`).
It also uses, references or redistributes material from the following projects.

## OpenThoughts-Agent — Apache-2.0

- Dataset: `open-thoughts/OpenThoughts-Agent-SFT-100K` (and three sibling pools used during
  reconnaissance). No raw dataset shards are redistributed here; `pipeline/download_pool.py`
  fetches them from Hugging Face at a pinned revision and verifies every shard against its
  LFS SHA256.
- Upstream repository: https://github.com/open-thoughts/OpenThoughts-Agent (Apache-2.0).
  Three files under `audit/` are unmodified upstream snapshots, kept only as provenance for
  the label-recovery claim; they are identified as such in `audit/README.md`.
- Derived text: `prepared/review/` contains rendered **excerpts of the released dataset**
  (full trajectory transcripts of the 299 sampled rows) in escaped, offline HTML. They are
  redistributed under the same Apache-2.0 terms as the source dataset, for audit purposes.
  Nothing in this repository executes the shell commands contained in those transcripts.

## Berkeley Function Calling Leaderboard (BFCL) / gorilla — Apache-2.0

- Project: https://github.com/ShishirPatil/gorilla (Apache-2.0).
- `pipeline/eval_bfcl.py` and `pipeline/eval_bfcl_local.py` import the official
  `bfcl_eval` package rather than vendoring it. `pipeline/fetch_assets.py` downloads the
  pinned wheel (`bfcl_eval==2026.3.23`) and unpacks it into `.third_party/`, which is not
  committed. Evaluation data, prompt templates, decoders and AST checkers therefore come
  from the official package, unmodified.
- We do not pip-install the package because its dependency list includes every vendor API
  client (anthropic, cohere, mistralai, google-genai, boto3, ...) which this work does not use.
  See `09_evaluation_sensitivity.md` §1.

## Qwen3-4B — Apache-2.0

- Model: https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-4B. Weights are not redistributed;
  `pipeline/fetch_assets.py` downloads them into `smoke/model/` (git-ignored).

## Note on credential-like strings

The released agent trajectories occasionally contain credential-shaped text as part of the
task content (for example a truncated sample RSA key inside a coding task). Those strings
originate in the public upstream dataset. Raw row dumps are git-ignored; the rendered review
pages under `prepared/review/` inherit them from the source data. No live credential or
access token is used by, or stored in, this repository.
